# W1 misuse: $h.write on a READ handle is a runtime error, identical in both
# engines. `stdin` is a read-only Handle (a reader, no writer), so writing to it
# aborts. The "before" line is flushed to stdout first (the gate compares stdout
# + exit code: both engines print "before" then exit non-zero). The error text on
# stderr differs between engines (Go message vs native "panic: ..."), so there is
# deliberately NO .stderr sidecar.
sub main(): Int {
    print("before")
    stdin.write("x")
    print("unreachable")
    0
}
